From: GameShellNeo development <gameshellneo@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] PM: sleep: report wakeup policy enable failures through sysfs

A failed wakeup-source registration leaves power/wakeup disabled, but the
attribute currently reports the entire request as successful. Return the
existing device_set_wakeup_enable() error to the caller.

Preserve idempotent enabled writes without requiring a new allocation.
Observe the existing source while holding power.lock, release the lock before
allocation, and accept -EEXIST when another sysfs writer attached a source in
between. Internal allocator, attach, detach and source-lifetime APIs are
unchanged. Concurrent writes retain their normal observation/attachment
ordering; this does not serialize every policy request.

This candidate is opt-in and is not in the image patch queue.

---
--- a/drivers/base/power/sysfs.c
+++ b/drivers/base/power/sysfs.c
@@ -331,16 +331,30 @@
 static ssize_t wakeup_store(struct device *dev, struct device_attribute *attr,
 			    const char *buf, size_t n)
 {
+	bool enabled;
+	int ret;
+
 	if (!device_can_wakeup(dev))
 		return -EINVAL;
 
-	if (sysfs_streq(buf, _enabled))
-		device_set_wakeup_enable(dev, 1);
-	else if (sysfs_streq(buf, _disabled))
-		device_set_wakeup_enable(dev, 0);
-	else
+	if (sysfs_streq(buf, _enabled)) {
+		/* Repeated requests must not depend on another allocation. */
+		spin_lock_irq(&dev->power.lock);
+		enabled = !!dev->power.wakeup;
+		spin_unlock_irq(&dev->power.lock);
+		if (enabled)
+			return n;
+
+		ret = device_set_wakeup_enable(dev, 1);
+		/* Another writer may have attached its source meanwhile. */
+		if (ret == -EEXIST)
+			ret = 0;
+	} else if (sysfs_streq(buf, _disabled)) {
+		ret = device_set_wakeup_enable(dev, 0);
+	} else {
 		return -EINVAL;
-	return n;
+	}
+	return ret < 0 ? ret : n;
 }
 
 static DEVICE_ATTR_RW(wakeup);
